<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="64504" href="schedule/2015/fall/ATMS/491/64504.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2015" href="schedule/2015.xml">2015</calendarYear><term id="120158" href="schedule/2015/fall.xml">Fall 2015</term><subject id="ATMS" href="schedule/2015/fall/ATMS.xml">Atmospheric Sciences</subject><course id="491" href="schedule/2015/fall/ATMS/491.xml">Adv Topics in Atmospheric Sci</course></parents><sectionNumber>RS </sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Physical Oceanography</sectionTitle><creditHours>4 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>The course will include descriptive and quantitative analyses of the physical properties and dynamics of the global oceans.  Key concepts will include: physical properties of sea water, wind-driven and themahaline circulations, heat storage and transport, vertical diffusion and upwelling, water mass formations, ocean-atmosphere interactions, equatorial dynamics, and the role of the ocean in Earth's climate system.</sectionText><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2015-08-24Z</startDate><endDate>2015-12-09Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="DIS">Discussion/Recitation</type><start>12:30 PM</start><end>01:50 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>109</roomNumber><buildingName>Atmospheric Sciences Bldg</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Sriver" firstName="R">Sriver, R</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>